==Icelandic==
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|stóll|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*stōlaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*stāl-||frame, rack, stand}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[stoutl]|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|outl|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|stóls|stólar}}

# [[chair]]

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-m-s1|st|ó|l|l}}
----

==Old Norse==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|12th century Icelandic}} {{IPA|/ˈstoːlː/|lang=non}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|non}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*stōlaz||stool, chair, throne}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term/t|ang|stōl}}, {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{term/t|ofs|stōl}}, {{etyl|osx|-}} {{term/t|osx|stōl}}, {{etyl|odt|-}} {{term/t|odt|stuol}}, {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term/t|goh|stuol}}, {{etyl|got|-}} {{term/t|got|𐍃𐍄𐍉𐌻𐍃|tr=[[stols#Gothic|stōls]]|sc=Goth}}. Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|non}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*stāl-||frame, rack, stand}}. The second meaning is a calque of {{etyl|la|-}} {{term/t|la|sēdēs||seat}}, while the third is presumably a calque of {{etyl|la|-}} {{term/t|la|thronī||the Thrones}}.

====Noun====
{{non-noun|m|stóls|stólar}}
# a [[stool]], [[chair]], [[throne]]
#* ''Saga Hákonar Hákonarsonar'' 254, in '''1835''', [[w:Finnur_Magnússon|F. Magnússon]], [[w:Carl_Christian_Rafn|C. C. Rafn]], ''Fornmanna sögur'', Volume X. Copenhagen, page [http://books.google.com/books?id=Wy8IAAAAIAAJ&pg=PA16 16]:
#*: {{...}} þar tvískipat eptir endilöngu, voru skipaðir XIII '''stólar'''.
#*:: {{...}} ''there along the entire length [of the king's court] were set in two thirteen '''chairs'''.''
# {{context|ecclesiastic|lang=non}} [[bishop|bishop's]] [[residence]], [[see]]
#* ''Guðmundar saga'' 68, in '''1858''', [[w:Jón_Sigurðsson|J. Sigurðsson]], [[w:Guðbrandur_Vigfússon|G. Vigfússon]], ''Biskupa sögur'', Volume I. Copenhagen, page [http://books.google.com/books?id=py4PAAAAIAAJ&pg=PA508 508]:
#*: {{...}} ok fór hann heim til '''stóls''' sins; {{...}} 
#*:: {{...}} ''and came back to [the bishop's] '''see''';'' {{...}} 
# {{context|Christianity, in the plural|lang=non}} the [[throne|Thrones]] (a [[class]] of [[angel]]s)
#* ''Íslensk Hómilíubók'', in '''1864''', C. R. Unger, ''Gammel Norsk Homiliebog''. Christiania, page [http://books.google.com/books?id=oWUAAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA185 185], lines 11-12:
#*: {{...}} þat ero englar oc hofuðenglar oc craftar, veldisenglar oc hofðingiar, drotnar oc '''stolar''', {{...}}
#*:: {{...}} ''there are angels and archangels and Powers, Virtues and Principalities, Dominions and '''Thrones''','' {{...}}

=====Declension=====
{{non-decl-m-a|stól|stól|ns=stóll}}

