===Etymology 2===
Probably from {{etyl|sla-pro|non}} {{term/t|sla-pro|*stolъ||table}}.

====Noun====
{{non-noun|m|stóls|stólar}}
# a [[table]] for [[eating]] and [[drinking]]
#* ''Bósa saga ok Herrauðs'' 12, in '''1830''', [[w:Carl_Christian_Rafn|C. C. Rafn]], ''Fornaldar sögur Nordrlanda'', Volume III, Copenhagen, page [http://books.google.com/books?id=M9sFAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA223 223]:
#*: {{...}} hann tók borðbúnað af '''stólnum''', ok kastaði upp í sængina, {{...}}
#*:: {{...}} ''he took the dishes from the '''table''' and threw them up in the bed sheets,'' {{...}}

=====Declension=====
{{non-decl-m-a|stól|stól|ns=stóll}}

===Etymology 3===
Presumably ultimately from {{etyl|grc|non}} {{term/t|grc|στόλος||army, fleet, troop}}.

====Noun====
{{non-noun|m|stóls|stólar}}
# a [[stock]] (especially of weapons and ships), [[host]], [[fleet]]
#* ''Saga Sverris konúngs'' 71, in '''1834''', [[w:Finnur_Magnússon|F. Magnússon]], [[w:Carl_Christian_Rafn|C. C. Rafn]], ''Fornmanna sögur'', Volume VIII, Copenhagen, page [http://books.google.com/books?id=tywIAAAAIAAJ&pg=PA177 177]:
#*: Í þenna tíma hafði Magnús konúngr einn allan skipa'''stólinn''', {{...}}
#*:: ''At that time had king Magnus an entire '''fleet''' of ships,'' {{...}}

=====Declension=====
{{non-decl-m-a|stól|stól|ns=stóll}}

